   "text": "The molecule is a maleimide\u2013PEG3\u2013Gly-Gly-Phe-Gly linker joined through an NH-CH2-O-CH2 spacer to an amino-fluoro camptothecin core (exatecan-like). I read it in these pieces, left to right:\n\n1. **Maleimide:** O=C1C=CC(=O)N1, with its nitrogen attached to a PEG3 chain, CCOCCOCCOCC.\n2. **Linker amide:** the chain ends in C(=O) bonded to NH, which starts the peptide.\n3. **Tetrapeptide:** Gly-Gly-Phe-Gly. The Phe benzyl group is on a hashed bond. Working through the geometry gives the L configuration, written `[C@@H]` with N listed first.\n4. **Spacer:** the last glycine's C(=O) links to NH-CH2-O-CH2, and this CH2 is attached to C7 of the camptothecin core.\n5. **Camptothecin core:**\n   - The benzo ring carries NH2 on the carbon nearer the C7 side and F on the carbon nearer the quinoline N.\n   - It is fused to the pyrrolo-quinoline system, which carries the pyridone C=O.\n   - The lactone ring ends in the quaternary carbon bearing OH (wedge) and ethyl (hash). Tracing the geometry from the drawing gives `[C@]` for the order of atoms in my SMILES.\n\nI checked ring closures and atom connectivity against the drawing by hand; I did not run a validator.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCOCCOCCOCCC(=O)NCC(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)NCC(=O)NCOCc1c2c(nc3cc(F)c(N)cc13)-c1cc3c(c(=O)n1C2)COC(=O)[C@]3(O)CC"
  }
